Package: terminal-system
Version: 1.1.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash, tmux, xclip
Maintainer: Franco Conidi aka edmond <fconidi@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://www.syslinuxos.com
Description: AI-assisted two-pane terminal (natural language -> shell commands)
 A tmux two-pane layout: the right pane takes instructions in natural
 language, an AI engine (Claude Code or Codex, called non-interactively
 and with no tool access of its own) translates each instruction into
 shell command(s), and those commands are typed into the left pane in
 real time.
 .
 Every command is confirmed manually by default; an opt-in auto-mode
 (":auto on") executes safe commands automatically, but a fixed set of
 dangerous patterns (rm -rf /, mkfs, dd onto /dev, fork bombs, and
 similar) always forces manual confirmation regardless of auto-mode.
 .
 Session instructions and commands are kept as context for follow-up
 instructions within the same session, and are never written to disk.
 .
 Requires the "claude" and/or "codex" CLI to already be installed and
 authenticated; neither is a hard package dependency since neither ships
 as a .deb on this system.
Installed-Size: 128
